I didn't write this code. All of it -- the SLIC/ folder and the
root-level driver scripts below -- is from the SLIC (Subcellular
Location Image Classifier) toolbox, from Robert F. Murphy's lab at
Carnegie Mellon:

  Boland, M.V., Murphy, R.F. "A Neural Network Classifier Capable of
  Recognizing the Patterns of All Major Subcellular Structures in
  Fluorescence Microscope Images of HeLa Cells." Bioinformatics 17.12
  (2001): 1213-1223.

I only swapped the file paths in these Murphy Lab templates to point
to my own gastric cancer image dataset -- I didn't change the logic:

  createproc_GC_AZ521.m, createproc_GC_HS746T.m, createproc_GC_MKN45.m,
  createproc_GC_MKN7.m, createproc_GC_SCH.m, createproc_GC_SNU1.m,
  createproc_GC_TMK1.m, handseg_GC_AZ521.m, handseg_GC_HS746T.m,
  handseg_GC_MKN45.m, handseg_GC_MKN7.m, handseg_GC_SCH.m,
  handseg_GC_SNU1.m, handseg_GC_TMK1.m, handseg.m,
  feat_combine_auto.m, feat_lowcommon.m, feat_lowcommon_field.m,
  TTest_Features.m, TTest_FeaturesPAPER.m, Runner_0703_2013.m,
  SC_CellLevelFeatures_Wrapper.m

`ContrastStretchNorm.m` is by Sergei Koptenko, Resonant Medical,
Montreal, QC (March 2006) -- also not mine.

What's actually mine: running this code on my dataset, and the output
-- the T-Test results in `results/` and the reports in `reports/`.

No warranty. Ask the original authors for terms on reusing their code.
